\newlabel{fig:appendix_representative_posteriors}{{8}{28}{Representative calibrated event-time posteriors. Dashed black lines denote the true RT, and dotted colored lines denote model-specific posterior means. The examples illustrate why scalar RT alone is insufficient: models can agree on the mean while assigning very different posterior width, or disagree strongly because the posterior is multimodal or skewed}{figure.8}{}}
